      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_launcher_1a725a3958001b044eb14d96569b77f115" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int Launcher::run</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>run</name>
        <qualifiedname>Launcher::run</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Starts the target and returns its exit code. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Windows creates the target suspended, sends its process ID, and reads the reply. When the reply says didAttach, it waits for the target to exit. Otherwise it terminates the target. When the target cannot be created, it sends an error message. macOS opens the reply FIFO with close-on-exec. It spawns the target with POSIX_SPAWN_START_SUSPENDED. It watches the exit of the target with a kqueue. It sends the process ID of the target. When the reply says didAttach, it waits for the exit event and returns the exit code of the target. A target that a signal killed gives 128 plus the signal number. Otherwise it kills the target with SIGKILL. When the spawn fails, it sends an error message.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>The exit code of the target on both platforms. failedLaunchExitCode when the target does not start or does not attach. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
